{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["He sat on the bed — his legs were down on the ground, which is why it is written before us: ״ויוצא יוסף אותם מעם ברכיו״, and also to indicate the strength of Yaakov, that all the words of his testament he delivered while sitting and his legs on the ground, until he finished all his words, and afterward ״ויאסף רגליו אל המטה״ — he drew them onto the bed, as in ״ואספתו אל תוך ביתך״, and no person gathers them home."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "The final clause ואין איש מאסף אותם הביתה is rendered hyper-literally; the referent of 'them' and the force of the comparison are textually obscure."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:29.027648306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}